B.ut=new A.ag(B.kw,["Back","Continue","Save","required","{field} is required","This field is required","Uploading...","Upload","Replace","You must be logged in as a driver.","Coming soon","GOOD MORNING","Select language","Notifications","No notifications","Change profile photo","Logout","Profile photo updated.","Failed to upload profile photo: {error}","Could not read image bytes from file picker.","Hi {name}, \ud83d\udc4b","welcome to {company}","We\u2019re happy to have you on board. Let\u2019s get started!","CODRIVER","YOUR ADDRESS","YOUR ORIGIN","UNIFORM","Street, Housenumber","Postal Code","City","Country","Your Birthday","City of Birth","State of Birth","Nationality (ID CARD) (Country name)","choose your cloth size","S / M / L / XL","choose your shoe size","e.g. 42","other wishes / notes","WORK PERMIT","which kind of work permit do you have to work in Germany","German ID Card","EU ID Card","WORK VISA for Germany","YOUR WORK PERMIT","please upload your document","Make sure the photo is fully visible, high-quality, and taken from a top-down angle","upload your file","JPG, JPEG, HEIC, PDF format up to 50 mb","select expiry date","ID Card, Passport","ID CARD","PASSPORT","OR","YOUR PASSPORT","YOUR ID CARD","FRONTSIDE","BACKSIDE","YOUR DRIVERS LICENSE","upload your file (front)","upload your file (back)","JPG, JPEG, HEIC, PNG (not PDF)","TAX DOCUMENT","please upload your tax ID document","upload tax ID","PDF, JPG, PNG\u2026 up to 50 MB","IBAN","License expiry date","Select expiry date","Uploaded documents","No documents uploaded yet.","Work permit / residence permit","Tax ID document","Insurance","Other document","Driver license (front)","Driver license (back)","ID card (front)","ID card (back)","Passport (front)","Passport (back)","Error loading reports: {error}","Your DSP has not uploaded any scorecard reports yet.","SCORECARD WEEK {week}","Week {week}, {year}","No scores for this period yet.","No drivers match this filter.","(No Name)","Company Score","My Score","Select period","Weekly view","Best DA of the Month","Best DA of the Year","Week","Total Score","Rank in station","Status","Rank","Score","Name","Delivered","Rank in AION","{rank} of {total}","No score found for your driver ID in this week.","SCORE","VALUE","PRO TIP","Delivery Completion Rate","Delivery Not Received","Loss on Route","Proof of Delivery","Customer Contact","Customer Experience","Customer Delivery Failures","Delivery Completion Rate (DCR) measures how many planned stops were successfully completed.","Maintain a consistent pace throughout the route and avoid unnecessary detours.",'Delivery Not Received (DNR) Is when you have delivered a package, and clicked "Swipe to finish" button confirming you have delivered the package but the costumer has not received the package due to number of reasons: Package theft, box being empty of the package items and also wrong delivery to the wrong address. Every Tuesday you will receive pictures of every DNR you have received during the week.',"It is very important and to avoid this you simply should inform the costumer beforehand that you are soon going to their house/business and ONLY ring the bell with their nameplate on it","Loss on Route (LoR) tracks lost or damaged packages during the route.","Handle packages carefully and organise the van so that parcels do not get damaged.","Proof of Delivery (POD) measures correct scan and delivery confirmations.","Always scan the package at the door and ensure the correct drop location.","Contact Compliance (CC) Meaning how many times you have reached out to the costumer about their delivery, be it via message or a phone call. The less you interact with the costumer, the less scores you will get in the scorecard and we should keep this section as high as possible because it is actually one of the the easiest categories and it helps a lot in your overall score.","Send messages or call customers when necessary to avoid missed deliveries.","Customer Experience (CE) represents how satisfied customers are with your deliveries.","Be friendly, punctual and careful with parcels to improve customer feedback.","Customer Delivery Failures (CDF) tracks serious delivery issues.","Analyse failed deliveries and learn from patterns to avoid repeating mistakes.","January","February","March","April","May","June","July","August","September","October","November","December","Jan","Feb","Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug","Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec","Fantastic","Great","Fair","Poor","Fantastic Plus","Fantastic","Great","Fair","Poor","at","of","Month","KW","FAQ","Search\u2026","No results.","What is most important about your daily task?","Delivering packages in quality and in good behavior.","What should you not do in case of problems with the costumer?","DO NOT try to handle the situation yourself and inform a dispatcher on-duty instead. We will try to talk to the costumer for you and avoid any bad consequences from Amazon due to costumer complaints. We are here for you!","What if the situation has already escalated and the costumer is not happy for whatever happened?","It's never too late to fix any mistakes. Still call us and we will try to fix the mistake with the costumer. Better late than ever.","What is more important, Quantity (speed of delivering as many stops as possible) or Quality?","Quality! Always quality! Follow costumer's instructions and DO NOT leave the package in unsafe locations, just because you are behind with your stops."],t.w)
